# @Fn in TypeAssert position: [@Fn 42] passes because @Fn resolves to TypeValue.Var
# (conservative: unknown type passes all values at runtime).
#
# TypeNode.Callable covers callable values; @Fn is a type annotation on the function
# type constructor, which the tycon_env maps to TypeValue.Var (the unknown TypeValue)
# rather than a structural function-type constraint. unknown_type_val() is consistent
# with all values under AGT — so Int(42) passes, not because @Fn accepts Ints, but
# because the runtime cannot enforce @Fn constraints without a resolved TypeValue.
[@Fn 42]
=== out
Int(42)
